# Cursor Rules for MyMasjidApp

## Code Quality Principles

- Prefer clarity and maintainability over cleverness
- Follow existing project conventions
- Keep functions small and single-purpose
- Do not invent APIs or dependencies
- Validate inputs and handle errors explicitly
- Refactor before rewriting
- Explain reasoning when suggesting changes

## Project-Specific Guidelines

### Code Style
- Use ES modules (import/export)
- Follow existing file structure (middleware, routes, controllers, services, utils)
- Maintain clear separation of concerns

### Error Handling
- Always use explicit try-catch blocks where errors may occur
- Provide meaningful error messages
- Use the project's error handler middleware

### Security
- Validate and sanitize all inputs
- Follow existing security middleware patterns (helmet, CORS, rate limiting)
- Never expose sensitive information in error messages

### Database
- Use the existing database connection pool
- Validate database inputs before queries
- Handle connection errors gracefully

### Function Design
- Single responsibility principle - one function, one purpose
- Keep functions focused and testable
- Use descriptive function and variable names

